WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.429 align:start position:0%
 
I was suffering from post-traumatic  stress disorder depression and grief I  was going downhill fast  ketamine's use as a transformer of mood  is only discovered in the late 90s and  people were very incredulous it's an  anesthetic how could it have anything to  do with mood what is actually happening  in the brain when a person takes this  drug I'm always a little nervous before  the injection because I know I have no  control over what my mind is going to  think about the trauma that I'm dealing  with basically unthinkable but I've lost  both of my children to suicide my  youngest son Dylan knew that his life  mattered that he mattered that he had a  voice and unfortunately his impulsive  nature caused him to go in and shoot  himself and end his life when I found  him I screamed uncontrollably what I saw  nobody should see I ran out of the house  hidden trapped back in to make sure he  wasn't wasn't still alive even though  it's physically impossible basically  like what I looked up I hired a grief  counselor immediately I hired the best  post traumatic stress disorder counselor  I could find and I did pull myself out  of it I did reengage and I had an older  son who's still with his mum and I  worried about him because he didn't go  to counseling and he held things in he  didn't share but he kept saying he was  fine and we were about to go to the  edmonton oilers playoff game with my dad  and my sister because I really believed  in trying to unite the family start  having us live our lives again that was  my obligation to others friends and  family and my son my son was clearly  depressed but he denied it  l'Damian before he was supposed to go  back to see his mother he called me on a  bike ride to tell me that he loved me  and I knew something was wrong when he  asked me how long it was gonna be it  reminded me of my other son when he  asked me the same question when I got  home a year ago about today I found my  other son dead of a gunshot wound  [Music]  needless to say I fell apart  brought in spiritual leaders I brought  in other counselors any ideas that  people had that could help me get a grip  of my life cuz for the first 4 months I  didn't care if I was alive I didn't care  if I died I didn't think it mattered I  had no hope I had no purpose  it was empty without my kids I first  went to some grief recovery centers I  went to a brain scanning clinic I signed  up with an EMDR specialist I was  severely depressed trying to get out of  it and I wanted to try to make some  progress on my own before I came to do  the ketamine and I wanted to get through  Christmas so having have lost one son  and knowing the worst date is Christmas  not the birth date not the anniversary  dated that Christmas is the worst date  if you've lost a child I knew they had  that coming and I didn't want to be  doing this or have just done it and then  get whacked again so I knew to get  through Christmas if I could get through  Christmas early January I'm flying back  into LA and I'm gonna come and spend two  weeks and do this treatment and I got  through Christmas and I made it here  [Music]  it's known as Special K a psychedelic  drug popular in dance clubs but doctors  say this same drug ketamine approved as  animal tranquilizer and anaesthetic can  also be a lifesaver when used to treat  severe depression when nothing else  works one small study found ketamine  decreased suicidal thoughts almost  immediately in 50% of patients most  antidepressants take weeks  tom was pretty troubled when he came to  us he was not dealing it all well Tom  really was blaming himself a lot for  that and we're suffering a great deal of  guilt and remorse pretty unsure about  whether he wanted to continue living he  had a very rough and contentious first  infusion by the day after his second  infusion he was really just singing the  praises of the treatment ketamine was  found to be profoundly effective  anesthetic given us a lump or bolus it  was only when people began to give it in  a very gradual way and its sub  anesthetic doses that we realized what  an amazing mood elevator and reversal  suicidality it is starts a chain  reaction it actually caused new growth  in connections in the brain and in  receptor density among those connections  the patient who has an infusion  experiences a disassociative state does  not have true hallucinations you may see  things that aren't there but he knows  that they're not there this association  can be very mild like when you're  waiting to pay at the grocery store  you're thinking about what you're going  to do tonight your mind and body are  sort of separate a lot of patients tell  us that they're able to do really  important internal work while they're  having an infusion it can be really  therapeutic for them to have a really  objective perspective on their life and  this dissociation that dr. Mendel is  talking about of course it's very  important we're big advocates of talk  therapy and for them to work through  some of these things with a professional  it's a treatment it's not a cure  it will not stand alone for me I'm  always a little nervous before the  injection because I know I have no  control over what my mind is going to  think about and it can go from very  pleasant the very scary I know at the  end I'm going to feel better I'm going  to say it's an out-of-body experience  I'm present watching myself but it's not  in a dimension that I can explain they  actually let me know that I matter that  I am good enough they gave me tools to  discuss with my conventional  psychologist  [Music]  I had moments of emotional pain from my  loss that I understood why somebody  would want to take their life and for  whatever reason something changed in me  that made me go from I don't care if I  live to I don't want to die and now  because of these treatments I can now go  and share my story and let people know  that life is worth living that as bad as  it gets us as painful it gets we do have  a choice and we have freedom to make  that choice but I can go out and help  other people possibly and whether I'm  successful or not doesn't matter I'm at  least gonna try to do that I'm gonna try  to give back with this clinics giving me  my life  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]

